WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.650
In comics' Golden Age, Dr. Fate committed
at least two genocides.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:10.690
In More Fun Comics #61, Dr. Fate is flying
through space when he sees "a strange nebula"

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.740
with a flaming globe at its core hanging around
Earth.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.180
Somehow, this breaks Earth's orbit around
the sun, almost freezing the planet before

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.199
Dr. Fate destroys the nebula with an "atom
shatterer" he "found on distant Uranus."

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:27.410
But then he finds a whole fleet of nebulae
coming for the earth and traces them to what

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:29.280
he calls "a pirate planet."

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.180
So Dr. Fate throws the whole planet into the
sun and kills everybody on it.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:40.280
You'd think one genocide's already too many,
but Dr. Fate goes for another in More Fun #65.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.250
The fish-men of Nyarl-Amen, who look kind
of like reverse mermaids, rise out of the

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.820
sea to conquer the earth.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.620
Fate hunts down their underwater city and
blows it to smithereens.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.390
The narration assures readers that "its fallen
ruins shelter no single thread of life except

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.340
a fish or two."

